A resumed thread is made ready but not put on a queue.
It would never get the processor;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on a queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place of a ready thread that may run waits on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@ static int op_thread(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, uint3
             return KERR_STATE;
         }
         target->flags &= (uint8_t)~THREAD_FAULTED;
-        sched_ready(target);
+        target->state = THREAD_READY;
         return KERR_OK;
     case OP_THREAD_STOP:
         arg[1] = sched_stop(target);
